   "end": 512
  },
  "info": "Vocoder: long chords, played by short stabs.\n\npad    the carrier: Am9, Fmaj9, Cmaj9 and G9, two bars each, a bright saw chord that holds and swells. Its Out node has `master` off, so it is not in the mix: only the vocoder hears it.\ntalk   the voice: short comb-resonator stabs, a different pitch of resonance every hit, so each one has its own colour. Not in the mix either (Out `master` off): only the vocoder hears it.\nvox    the vocoder. Two sidechain nodes carry the finished sound of talk (voice) and of pad (carrier) into it: the stabs' spectrum is measured in 10 bands and the chord is shaped by it, so the chord is heard only when a stab opens it, and in the colour of that stab.\n\nEight sparse bars, sixteen busy ones, eight sparse again, from the Node Sequencer (steps A and B pick which rhythm drives the stabs). Try the vocoder's Shf column (formant shift) and Rel while it plays.",
